WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:35.208
<b>Here, Lord Krishna begins to explain </b>
<b>Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

2
00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:37.291
<b>Its simple meaning is</b>

3
00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:44.083
<b>performing one's duty with knowledge and </b>
<b>awareness, without desiring any fruits of action.</b>

4
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:50.791
<b>Lord Krishna explains here</b>

5
00:00:50.791 --> 00:00:55.583
<b>that his analysis of the difference between</b>
<b>soul and body, which he has presented so far,</b>

6
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:58.666
<b>follows one branch of philosophy.</b>

7
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.791
<b>This branch is called Sankhya.</b>

8
00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:06.625
<b>And now here, Krishna begins to explain</b>
<b>about Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

9
00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:07.750
<b>It means,</b>

10
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:13.833
<b>with complete awareness, without desiring any </b>
<b>fruits of action, continuing to perform one's duties.</b>

11
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.541
<b>Nishkama Karma Yoga</b>

12
00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:20.833
<b>is capable of taking a human to</b>
<b> their highest spiritual level.</b>

13
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:24.458
<b>Krishna has used another term here,</b>

14
00:01:24.458 --> 00:01:25.791
<b>Buddhi Yoga,</b>

15
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:31.791
<b>by which he means performing actions</b>
<b>in this world using one's intellect,</b>

16
00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.291
<b>knowing that</b>

17
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:37.625
<b>human's real existence is spiritual, not physical.</b>

18
00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:41.708
<b>Here, continuous emphasis </b>
<b>has been placed on action.</b>

19
00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:46.208
<b>Krishna doesn't want Arjuna to</b>
<b>think of renunciation or asceticism,</b>

20
00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:53.541
<b>rather it would be right for Arjuna to perform</b>
<b>his duties with the awareness that he is a soul.</b>

21
00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:58.458
<b>With this understanding, Arjuna will be</b>
<b>able to fulfill his duties completely,</b>

22
00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:02.125
<b>while also staying away from sin.</b>

23
00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:09.208
<b>Knowledge!</b>

24
00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:12.541
<b>What is the importance of knowledge?</b>

25
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:17.500
<b>How does it elevate our life's standard?</b>

26
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:23.208
<b>If some knowledge doesn't make us </b>
<b>better parents, a better spouse,</b>

27
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:24.708
<b>a better friend,</b>

28
00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:28.958
<b>a better person</b>

29
00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:32.708
<b>is such knowledge useful?</b>

30
00:02:32.708 --> 00:02:38.291
<b>You might think, why so many questions at once?</b>

31
00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.416
<b>The meaning behind these questions is</b>

32
00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:47.083
<b>that merely acquiring knowledge</b>
<b>doesn't make us better</b>

33
00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:54.166
<b>we become better when we can implement </b>
<b>that knowledge in our personal lives.</b>

34
00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:57.666
<b>When we can use it in life.</b>

35
00:02:57.666 --> 00:02:59.125
<b>For example.</b>

36
00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:01.625
<b>The water you drink </b>

37
00:03:01.625 --> 00:03:03.458
<b>contains molecules, </b>

38
00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:04.625
<b>atoms,</b>

39
00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:07.375
<b>and some microorganisms too.</b>

40
00:03:07.375 --> 00:03:09.333
<b>Good knowledge.</b>

41
00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:15.833
<b>But can you use just this knowledge?</b>

42
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:16.583
<b>Yes,</b>

43
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:18.625
<b>if you're a scientist,</b>

44
00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:20.291
<b>a chemist,</b>

45
00:03:20.291 --> 00:03:24.750
<b>then perhaps you can use this knowledge,</b>

46
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:31.500
<b>because then you know not just the words, </b>
<b>definitions, and information,</b>

47
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.666
<b>but also the technique of </b>
<b>their practical application.</b>

48
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:42.583
<b>I explained to Arjuna the difference between </b>
<b>body and soul in detail,</b>

49
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:43.666
<b>but</b>

50
00:03:43.666 --> 00:03:47.833
<b>now is the time when I must explain to him</b>

51
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:53.583
<b>how to apply all these things in practical life.</b>

52
00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:57.875
<b>How to implement this knowledge. 	 </b>

53
00:03:57.875 --> 00:03:59.916
<b>Stay with me,</b>

54
00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:03.125
<b>this is for you too.</b>

55
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:04.375
<b>And yes,</b>

56
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:07.833
<b>what use is mere verbal knowledge?</b>

57
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:12.750
<b>Whenever you learn something, don't stop there.</b>

58
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:19.291
<b>Implement any learning in life,</b>
<b> only then will you benefit.</b>

59
00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:26.291
<b>These teachings of the Gita too will benefit you </b>
<b>only when you apply them in life.</b>

60
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.083
<b>In society,</b>

61
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:33.208
<b>in family,</b>

62
00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:35.750
<b>you'll surely meet people</b>

63
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.791
<b>who give suggestions with good intentions,</b>

64
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:47.708
<b>but cannot explain how to implement </b>
<b>that suggestion, how to use it.</b>

65
00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:50.291
<b>For example, this suggestion,</b>

66
00:04:50.291 --> 00:04:52.875
<b>"Take care of your health."</b>

67
00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:55.125
<b>This suggestion is good,</b>

68
00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:57.416
<b>but incomplete.</b>

69
00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:00.375
<b>It becomes complete when along with it,</b>

70
00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:05.333
<b>there's discussion of some methods </b>
<b>to maintain health,</b>

71
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:08.666
<b>like exercise regularly,</b>

72
00:05:08.666 --> 00:05:13.166
<b>maintain a balanced diet, and so on.</b>

73
00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:18.000
<b>You understand, right? What I'm trying to say.</b>

74
00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.000
<b>If I just explain to Arjuna the</b>
<b>difference between soul and body,</b>

75
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:30.041
<b>and don't show him the path to implement </b>
<b>this knowledge, to put it to use,</b>

76
00:05:30.041 --> 00:05:33.250
<b>then this knowledge might be incomplete.</b>

77
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.708
<b>Now is the time</b>

78
00:05:34.708 --> 00:05:38.250
<b>to explain its practical applications.</b>

79
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.958
<b>You too, consider this,</b>

80
00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:45.666
<b>if you're giving someone advice,</b>
<b>don't leave it incomplete.</b>

81
00:05:45.666 --> 00:05:50.000
<b>Try to rise above verbal knowledge</b>

82
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.583
<b>and explain how to use that knowledge in</b>
<b>practical life, its benefits, some examples</b>

83
00:05:55.583 --> 00:05:58.833
<b>if you can explain these too,</b>

84
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:01.375
<b>it will be more effective.</b>

85
00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:07.583
<b>At workplace,</b>

86
00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:09.208
<b>what to do? </b>

87
00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>This is generally known to all,</b>

88
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.125
<b>but how to do that work well?</b>

89
00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:20.500
<b>Here sometimes mistakes do happen.</b>

90
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.083
<b>For example</b>

91
00:06:22.083 --> 00:06:27.708
<b>say you're in a senior managerial position</b>
<b> in an organization,</b>

92
00:06:27.708 --> 00:06:31.625
<b>so you must have some colleagues </b>
<b>appointed under you.</b>

93
00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:34.000
<b>What to do is clear.</b>

94
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.333
<b>Assign work portions to colleagues and </b>
<b>ensure their completion.</b>

95
00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.708
<b>But how to do this, </b>

96
00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:47.041
<b>perhaps here you often fall short.</b>

97
00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:53.375
<b>You get entangled in taking on </b>
<b>others' small tasks yourself.</b>

98
00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:56.875
<b>Clarity of any task is necessary,</b>

99
00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:57.708
<b>but</b>

100
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:02.583
<b>its execution process is equally important.</b>

101
00:07:02.583 --> 00:07:05.541
<b>And if this process isn't understood,</b>

102
00:07:05.541 --> 00:07:07.208
<b>mistakes will happen,</b>

103
00:07:07.208 --> 00:07:08.416
<b>disagreements will arise,</b>

104
00:07:08.416 --> 00:07:09.708
<b>and perhaps</b>

105
00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:14.958
<b>you'll remain bound in a web of complications.</b>

106
00:07:14.958 --> 00:07:17.000
<b>"Karma-bandhan."</b>

107
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.833
<b>Arjuna too will remain bound in karma-bandhan</b>

108
00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:27.500
<b>if he understood the knowledge of </b>
<b>soul and life only theoretically, </b>

109
00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.125
<b>but not practically.</b>

110
00:07:31.125 --> 00:07:32.041
<b>Therefore,</b>

111
00:07:32.041 --> 00:07:37.625
<b>my goal now is to give him </b>
<b>practical understanding.</b>

112
00:07:37.625 --> 00:07:41.791
<b>In professional life, you too can learn from this.</b>

113
00:07:41.791 --> 00:07:44.333
<b>What to do, you know,</b>

114
00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:47.458
<b>your colleagues know too.</b>

115
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:49.416
<b>"How to do it."</b>

116
00:07:49.416 --> 00:07:51.458
<b>Know this yourself,</b>

117
00:07:51.458 --> 00:07:53.416
<b>and teach others too.</b>

